control: A job's last success is a run that succeeded or a unit of work made durable, and its series follow every way a run ends
removes: a job's last success is not emitted until its first success, so a job that never succeeds never ages
packages: ./worker/internal/schedule
tests: TestTheJobSeriesFollowEveryWayARunEnds
scheduled-count: no

